# Pairs with OwnerMonotonic. A reactivation does not rebuild the leaf's
# prepared buckets from the WAL, so a committed batch the owner was serving
# through its bucket reverts to the pre-saga row.
MODULE: OwnerMonotonicReactivationDropsBuckets
TARGET: OwnerMonotonic
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a reactivation loses the leaf's prepared buckets, so a visible commit reverts
PERTURBS: Reactivate

--- FIND
    /\ term[c][s] \/ \E k \in Keys : pend[c][s][k] = "mark"
    /\ term' = [term EXCEPT ![c][s] = FALSE]
    /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![c][s] = [k \in Keys |-> IF @[k] = "mark" THEN "none" ELSE @[k]]]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: replay does not rebuild the prepared buckets.
    /\ term' = [term EXCEPT ![c][s] = FALSE]
    /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![c][s] = [k \in Keys |-> "none"]]
--- END